cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Serenite: adaptive profiling and peer-matched online mental health support groups"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/taut0logy/Serenite"
abstract: >-
  Serenite is an open-source web platform that places people into small peer
  support groups and supports them between sessions. An adaptive assessment
  administers a graded-response item bank under a computerized adaptive testing
  policy, returning a six-domain latent trait vector used for matching and,
  separately, severity statements drawn only from three public-domain screening
  instruments with published cutoffs. Sessions run on a self-hosted mediasoup
  selective forwarding unit. Responses and diary entries are encrypted in the
  browser.
keywords:
  - computerized adaptive testing
  - item response theory
  - peer support
  - WebRTC
  - selective forwarding unit
  - mental health informatics
